WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.075
During the move, everything
runs side by side.

2
00:00:03.075 --> 00:00:06.507
The V P N stays for
applications not yet published,

3
00:00:06.507 --> 00:00:09.436
in split-include mode
where it supports it,

4
00:00:09.436 --> 00:00:13.705
so Private Access and the V P N
don't contend for the same routes;

5
00:00:13.705 --> 00:00:17.137
a V P N route is removed only
after the V P N's own logs

6
00:00:17.137 --> 00:00:21.238
show no traffic for that
application for ten business days.

7
00:00:21.238 --> 00:00:25.738
DirectAccess can't coexist with
Private Access on the same device.

8
00:00:25.738 --> 00:00:30.176
Where a proxy is set at the
operating system or browser level,

9
00:00:30.176 --> 00:00:35.413
Learn's P A C file guidance excludes
every F Q D N and I P the client tunnels.

10
00:00:35.413 --> 00:00:39.812
A third-party security service edge
kept for internet traffic follows

11
00:00:39.812 --> 00:00:43.913
its coexistence page on Learn, for
the bypasses in both directions.

12
00:00:43.913 --> 00:00:49.214
And branches: a remote network carries
the Microsoft and internet profiles, not

13
00:00:49.214 --> 00:00:54.675
Private Access, and applies only the baseline
profile, with no Conditional Access.

14
00:00:54.675 --> 00:00:57.915
That's a parity gap under
tick's Branch Office use case,

15
00:00:57.915 --> 00:01:01.597
so the guide keeps the client
on managed devices at branches,

16
00:01:01.597 --> 00:01:04.820
and uses the remote network
for devices without one.
